      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To expand the product \\((2x+3)(x+5)\\), we use the method of distributing or using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials).\n\n1. Start by multiplying the First terms in each binomial: \\[\n(2x)(x) = 2x^2\n\\]\n2. Then, multiply the Outer terms (leftmost term in the first binomial and rightmost term in the second binomial): \\[\n(2x)(5) = 10x\n\\]\n3. Next, multiply the Inner terms (rightmost term in the first binomial and leftmost term in the second binomial): \\[\n(3)(x) = 3x\n\\]\n4. Finally, multiply the Last terms in each binomial: \\[\n3(5) = 15\n\\]\n\nNow, combine all these products together: \n\\[\n2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15\n\\]\n\nCombine the like terms \\(10x\\) and \\(3x\\):\n\\[\n2x^2 + 13x + 15\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form of \\((2x+3)(x+5)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2x^2 + 13x + 15}\n\\]",
